+# ⭐⭐⭐ `TERRAINBLIT=1` (the DEFAULT) — THE TERRAIN BY BLITTER AREA FILL (RevsPlot.cpp §the blitter
+# terrain).  The CPU writes only each run's TOGGLE bits (where a pixel differs from its right
+# neighbour) into a chip-RAM buffer, and one exclusive-fill blit a block expands them into both PF1
+# planes while the CPU goes on with the frame.  CHOSEN AT RUN TIME: only on a 68000/68010 (a 68020+
+# paints faster itself — user decision); `TERRAINBLIT_FORCE=0|1` overrides, `g_terrainBlitOn` says
+# which ran.  `make TERRAINBLIT=0` compiles it out (the asm painter above).  Gate: `TERRAINCHECK=1` runs the per-cell oracle after the blit completes;
+# `TERRAINBLIT_SABOTAGE=N` (RevsPlot.cpp) and `SCANTOG_SABOTAGE=N` (scan_tog_m68k.s, the scan that
+# writes the toggles) build deliberate defects for it to catch.
+TERRAINBLIT ?= 1
+ifeq ($(TERRAINBLIT),1)
+EXTRA_DEFINES += -DREVS_TERRAIN_BLIT
+ASM_SRCS += $(AMIGA_SRC)/scan_tog_m68k.s
